In the lush, perilous jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, a diminutive Gnome Warlock named Fizzlewick trotted alongside his sultry Succubus pet, Lysandra. Despite the dangers lurking in the shadows, Fizzlewick felt invincible. Lysandra's seductive charm often distracted enemies, allowing Fizzlewick to cast his spells with ease. Yet, their bond was more than strategic; it was a friendship forged in the fires of adventure.

The answer to the riddle is: Warlocks are often seen with Voidwalkers due to the perception of safety and tanking capabilities, despite the Succubus's superior DPS and crowd control through Seduction. The misconception persists because Voidwalkers are seen as more traditional "pet tanks," while the Succubus's utility is often overlooked. [end of text]


